course: dictionary
lesson: 2289
title: One word, many teams
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer wants. Read «In 1970 an oxygen tank exploded on Apollo 13, and the crew worked out how to bring them home safely.» The crew are the people on the spacecraft, because they are the ones trying to bring the astronauts home.
explain: Now read «Damaged car batteries can catch fire and fire crews have special training for them.» Here crew means a team that does a job together. A fire crew is a team of firefighters. Ask yourself what job is being done, because that tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Crew can also be a doing word. «To crew» means to work as part of the crew of a boat or plane. If someone is crewing a boat, they are helping to sail it.
fact: A crew is a group of people who work together.
fact: A crew can be on a ship, a plane or a spacecraft, or it can be a team, such as a film crew or a road crew.
fact: «The flight crew look after passengers' safety» means the people who fly the plane keep the passengers safe.
fact: «Crewed» is the past form of the verb to crew, so it means worked as part of a crew.
fact: To choose the right meaning, ask what the people are doing and who they are working with.

exercise: «Most nature film crews follow a rule not to change what happens.» What is a crew in this sentence? | *A team that makes a film together | A group of penguins | A rope used to tie boats | A ship's sailors
exercise: «The captain and crew cheered when they saw land.» What does crew mean here? | A type of rope | *The people who work on the ship | A kind of storm | A loud song
exercise: «The students crewed the small boat across the lake.» What does crewed mean? | Stayed on the shore | Sank the boat | *Worked as part of the crew of the boat | Painted the boat

test: «Months later, starving and sick, the crew reached the Philippines.» Who are the crew in this sentence? | Fish caught in the sea | *The people who sailed the ship together | The king of the Philippines | Passengers who paid for a ticket
test: «The flight crew look after passengers' safety.» What do the flight crew do? | Drive the buses | Sell tickets at the airport | *Look after passengers' safety | Grow food for the passengers

exam: «The ___ of the spacecraft worked together to fix the broken oxygen tank.» Which word fits the gap? | *crew | crust | creek | crater
